---
source: src/cli/insights/mod.rs
assertion: revisionFrontiers insight section surfaces dominance-frontier leaders from the logical memory revision DAG
schema:
  item: ee.graph.revision_frontier.v1
  output: ee.insights.v1
contracts:
  - compute_workspace_revision_frontiers operates over the revision DAG built from logical memory IDs
  - items limited to MAX_SECTION_LIMIT, ranked by dominance_frontier_size descending
  - frontierRole is chain_root (no predecessors), interior (has successors), or chain_head (current, has predecessors)
  - stalePosture is superseded when the memory has successors in the revision DAG, otherwise current
  - affectedMemoryIds truncated to REVISION_FRONTIER_AFFECTED_ID_LIMIT; affectedMemoryIdsTruncated signals overflow
  - honest empty section returned when no revision DAG data is available or graph has zero nodes
  - evidence includes algorithm=dominance_frontiers and snapshotVersion from the latest revision DAG snapshot
evidence:
  - RevisionFrontierInsightInput.memory_id
  - RevisionFrontierInsightInput.frontier_role
  - RevisionFrontierInsightInput.stale_posture
  - RevisionFrontierInsightInput.dominance_frontier_size
  - RevisionFrontierInsightInput.affected_memory_ids
  - RevisionFrontierInsightInput.snapshot_version
  - item.rank
  - item.memoryId
  - item.frontierRole
  - item.stalePosture
  - item.dominanceFrontierSize
  - item.affectedMemoryIds
  - item.affectedMemoryIdsTruncated
  - item.evidence.schema
  - item.evidence.algorithm
  - item.evidence.snapshotVersion
verified_by:
  - cargo test --lib revision_frontiers_is_no_longer_placeholder_backed -- --nocapture
  - cargo test --lib revision_frontiers_section_from_inputs_emits_dominance_evidence -- --nocapture
  - cargo test --lib revision_frontiers -- --nocapture
